      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "The Chicago and North Western Railroad arrived in the 1850s, giving farmers a way to ship produce and linking Ridgefield to regional markets.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        10
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://grokipedia.com/page/ridgefield_illinois",
      "category": "transport",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "Ridgefield’s quiet rural feel is maintained by the absence of sidewalks, municipal water, sewer, police, or major commercial amenities.",
